WEBVTT

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.890
The forces of the Kingdom
of Elfrieden will return Van

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.060
to the Principality of Amidonia,
and return to their home country.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.690
As a condition of this return,
the Principality of Amidonia

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.360
is ordered to pay the Kingdom
of Elfrieden war reparations.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.410
Further, this payment is separate
from monies negotiated

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.910
for the return of prisoners of war.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.540
<i>"...Keep on going anyway"</i>

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:56.590
<i>Our bond strikes deep into my left breast</i>

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.440
<i>We enjoy a fleeting happiness</i>
<i>after weathering one fog,</i>

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.440
<i>until our vision becomes obscured again</i>

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.400
<i>Bitterly betrayed, we grow</i>
<i>disgusted by our destiny</i>

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.280
<i>But why does the dawn still come?</i>

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.620
<i>We close our eyes and try to remember</i>

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.960
<i>the chance of stopping, of never meeting</i>

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:37.550
<i>From boundless zero to infinity,</i>

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:43.060
<i>dreaming is the heartbeat of believing</i>

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.890
<i>We'll move along alone and in pairs</i>

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:53.020
<i>Don't stay put; our small,</i>
<i>though by no means helpless steps</i>

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.820
<i>will open uncharted territory</i>
<i>for each of us</i>

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:03.910
<i>Realize we will never again</i>
<i>let our dreams die on the vine</i>

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:10.710
<i>The tear tracks that run down</i>
<i>our cheeks are shooting stars</i>

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.550
<i>We're going to grab hold of them</i>

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:19.380
"Tyranny is More Terrible than Tigers"
Jeanne! What is the meaning of this?!

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.010
I returned your lands to you,
just as you requested.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:24.890
Are you joking?!

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:28.850
Having us pay reparations makes us
look like a defeated nation!

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:34.360
I'm afraid that's something unavoidable.
You lost your capital, after all.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.320
You're wrong! We haven't been beaten yet!

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.070
We just had one of our
cities conquered, that's all!

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:43.070
In that case, the empire will
withdraw from the dispute

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.830
between your two nations.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.080
Wha--?

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.040
You are free to go to war
or do whatever you like now.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.630
As I recall, you were unable to reclaim
your own capital, weren't you?

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.720
In that case, your side
is the loser in this war.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.680
As head of the Mankind Declaration,

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.390
the empire has settled the matter
of returning your national borders.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.100
We can intervene no further.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.860
B-But... reparations...

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:19.740
Julius, my sister, Maria,
is terribly saddened by this affair.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.530
As the treaty head, we cannot
overlook this act of aggression

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.660
that exploits a gap in the interpretation
of the Mankind Declaration.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:30.040
That was the act of
the previous ruler, Gaius.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.500
To ensure that member nations
do not produce those

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:38.380
who would commit such folly,
severe punishment is required.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.380
Your nation will set the precedent.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.600
And... if we refuse?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.020
Then the empire will
withdraw from this war,

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:54.690
and expel the Principality of Amidonia
from the Mankind Declaration.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:59.900
J-Just a moment, please!
Expel us from the Mankind Declaration?!

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.820
As I said earlier, your act of aggression

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.660
was a rather broad interpretation
of the Mankind Declaration.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.080
If we permit it, there will
likely be other countries

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.580
who will engage in the same kind of folly.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.380
I do not think my sister, Maria,
will approve of that.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.710
The Principality of Amidonia

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.720
is surrounded on four sides
by four other nations.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.720
If they lose the protections of
the Mankind Declaration now,

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.430
they could get preyed upon
by the other three countries.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:33.730
Gaius VIII maintained the country
on the north and south

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:36.230
by flexing his military might.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:40.780
One could say that Gaius did keep a
balanced diplomacy, after his own style.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.820
But does Julius possess the same acumen?

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.780
Your mediation plan... is accepted.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.870
A wise decision, Julius.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:59.290
Now then, let us proceed to start
negotiating specific amounts.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.000
The Kingdom of Elfrieden

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.550
requests two years' worth of the
Principality of Amidonia's annual budget.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:09.510
We do not intend for you to make
payment immediately, of course.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.560
We request ten years
of installment payments,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.890
all of which are to be made
in imperial coinage.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:17.020
Two years' worth of our annual budget?!

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.400
Do you think we will agree
to such an exorbitant amount?!

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.440
Julius,

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.950
they are requesting it
in imperial coinage.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.660
We would not be bothered
if you refuse their demands,

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:35.870
but if you do, you will not
be able to take Van back.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:46.800
More than 50% of Amidonia's annual budget
goes toward the military, right?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.010
And if we're taking 20%...

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:52.260
Part of the reason is to deprive them
of military funding, of course.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.560
Will Julius be able to
scale that back, though?

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.230
Jeanne, what if one of the
payments becomes overdue?

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:04.030
Then the empire will support the
Kingdom of Elfrieden's bid to annex Van.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.070
Julius, I believe you to be
a person of integrity,

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:11.990
but it's conceivable that someone
in your court could delay payment.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:14.370
Which is why I would like some collateral.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:19.120
Hmm? Collateral, you say?
What is it you want?

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.670
A Gemstone for broadcasts.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:27.220
Wha--?! There's only one
of them in the whole country!

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.220
You're planning on inciting the people!

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:32.720
All you have to do is change
the receivers' frequencies, right?

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.180
That would prevent them from receiving
transmissions from Elfrieden.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.440
That may be true...

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.600
Julius...

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.770
...I don't think the Gemstone
is enough collateral.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:47.240
To make up for the shortfall,

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:50.950
I'd like to take the books
from the castle's library.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:56.830
Ha! Oh, is that all?
You can have the books.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.380
Very well.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:06.000
All right, let's settle
the other matters before us.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.130
I would like our nation's soldiers

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:11.220
who are being held captive
by Elfrieden to be returned.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:14.600
Fine. But you will pay
a ransom for the nobles

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.930
and those of knight or higher rank.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:20.140
Furthermore, after your
country invaded ours,

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:23.400
we investigated those
who committed war crimes,

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.900
and compiled a list of names.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.690
We cannot consent to turning over
any captives who are on that list.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.200
Understood.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.200
We also request that those
whose names are on that list

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:41.040
but remain in your country
be turned over to us.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:46.090
Once that handover is completed,
we will start returning your prisoners.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.510
Is Roroa among your prisoners?

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:55.010
Roroa? Is that an acquaintance of yours?

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:58.680
Roroa Amidonia--my unworthy sister.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:02.480
O-Oh... Uh, I heard that she fled Van
before the fighting started,

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:05.270
along with other influential bureaucrats.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.150
All right, then.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.360
We can search for her on our end,
if you need.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.490
Not necessary.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:15.370
He's watching out for
a succession dispute.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:20.830
Despite her being one of his few
relatives left, now that Gaius is gone?

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:23.330
It happens a lot in royal families.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:27.790
Even in the Kingdom of Elfrieden,
there was an awful successorship struggle

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.170
until my mother took the throne.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:34.680
I get that. I just wish I didn't.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.930
In my view, as someone having no family,

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:40.770
I would think I'd at least take good care
of my one and only sister.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.850
Also, concerning General Margarita--

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:47.270
we would like to have her
remain in the kingdom.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:49.940
General Margarita Wonder?

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:54.150
If you will release five of the noblemen
you are holding for no ransom,

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.360
then we accept.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:56.610
Julius...

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:02.830
From what I hear, she worked with
the kingdom after the occupation.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:05.620
Isn't this a bit much
for your side to accept?

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:09.040
Giving her up in exchange
for a mere five noblemen is...

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.840
Very well. We accept your terms.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:18.930
She has been a fine general, but is she
really someone you want that badly?

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.890
Someone like you, who only judges
people by their military value,

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.390
probably wouldn't understand.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.670
In exchange for returning Van,

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:54.260
the Kingdom of Elfrieden receives
a great deal of compensation.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:59.470
In exchange for paying compensation,
Amidonia got Van back.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:02.180
And by acting as the mediator
of this dispute,

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.720
the empire has showed off its presence.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:07.520
I am satisfied to leave it at that.

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:11.400
What satisfaction is there in imposing
disadvantage on Amidonia?!

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.650
Excuse me!

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.660
Julius!

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.570
What?

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:26.120
Machiavelli, a political thinker in the
world I come from, said the following:

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.040
"Those who acquire a principality
with difficulty keep it with ease;

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.920
those who acquire a principality without
difficulty keep it only with difficulty."

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.590
Hmm? What is that supposed to mean?

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:38.930
I defeated you and obtained Van.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:44.100
I then purged the nobles, the knights,
and any other potential political foes.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.060
All on my own merits.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:51.480
So even if I were to continue to govern
Van, I would not have much trouble.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:55.940
But what about you?
After you return to power,

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:58.280
will you be able to govern
without any incident?

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:03.160
This was my country to begin with!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.410
You...

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.870
You used an outside force,

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.870
in the form of the empire's
authority, to take it back.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:15.960
What Machiavelli called "acquiring
a principality without difficulty."

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.920
He also said the following:

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:23.550
"One who becomes a prince without
difficulty must exercise great effort."

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.430
You must direct that effort
to helping your people--

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:27.430
Nobody asked you!

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.980
I wonder what the lords and
commoners of Amidonia will think

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:40.820
of the gentleman who could not
take back the capital on his own.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:45.200
He is a fool to ignore
your warning, Souma.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:12.980
We weren't here for very long, but now
that we're leaving, I'm going to miss it.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:15.230
Staying here would just be
a waste of war funds.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.190
A waste of time, as well.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.860
Your Majesty, our issues within
the kingdom remain untouched--

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.030
I know.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:26.240
Why does everyone look so sad?

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.830
They're probably anxious...

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.420
...over falling under Amidonian
reign once again.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:36.540
Anxious? But everything is
going back to the way it was.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.420
Yeah, that's why.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:43.380
They were living under oppression.
It's what they had come to expect.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:47.010
But by being placed under
the Kingdom's occupation,

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:50.180
they learned that they
could expect something else.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:55.900
You <i>did </i>allow them the freedom to
express their thoughts and feelings.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:58.440
Which is why they're now anxious
about whether or not

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:02.280
they're coming under an age
of oppression again.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.030
And in fact, they probably will.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:10.160
Knowing Julius, he's likely to crack
down on the relaxed mood here.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.500
Now that they've gotten
a taste of freedom,

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.790
they can't go back to their old lives.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.460
Almost like it's an addiction.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:23.470
You make a fair point, but isn't
there a better way to put it?

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:29.850
It's true, isn't it? Still, it's not that
easy to change the mindset of a nation.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:31.510
In the world I come
from we have a saying--

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:35.270
"Tyranny is more terrible than tigers."

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:38.060
Tyranny is more terrible than tigers?

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:43.610
It means that a bad government is
more dreadful than a man-eating tiger.

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:48.280
To the people of Van,
we might have been invading tigers.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:53.790
But we weren't tyrants. And now that
they know the tyrants are returning...

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:57.540
Ugh... the more I walk around with you,

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:01.040
the more I see the harsher
side of people's lives.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.170
Had enough yet?

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:04.760
--Bring it on!
--Bring it on, sire!

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.760
What's gotten into you, Aisha?

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.010
No path walked with
His Majesty is a hard one!

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:16.980
I feel the same way. I'll accept going
down any road as long as it's with you.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:19.310
I get nothing <i>but </i>hardship.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.060
Uh, right.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.450
Sister,

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:35.580
I have just returned from
the capital city of Van.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:40.380
I'm glad you're home, Jeanne.
How did everything go?

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.380
There was a little bit of trouble,

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:45.590
but things turned out the way
we hoped, for the most part.

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:50.800
The return of Van to the Principality
of Amidonia is already complete.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.560
Thank you for your efforts.
You have done well.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.890
Now, that's enough of work mode!

00:14:57.890 --> 00:14:59.140
S-Sister?

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:02.520
Welcome home, Jeanne!

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.650
Where is this coming from so suddenly?

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:07.150
This is inappropriate
behavior for an empress.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:12.820
I mean, I haven't seen your face
in some time, and I missed you.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:16.240
Everyone outside of family
treats me like the empress,

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:21.040
and my other sister just stays
locked up inside her laboratory.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:24.630
Don't "I mean" me.
We're not children anymore.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:26.000
Aww...

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:32.090
So anyhow, tell me!
What kind of man is this Souma?

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:34.220
Souma is...

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:36.060
What's he like?

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:42.560
The kind of man who keeps a bed
in the office, the same as you.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.810
Oh, my!

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:49.280
First of all, Souma is aware
of the empire's intentions,

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:52.490
and is not angry about the hero summoning.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.200
Thank goodness.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:57.490
He's also a very intelligent man.

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:00.910
He says that certain things are common
knowledge in the world he came from,

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:04.380
but comes up with one
innovation after another.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.670
I never would have thought
of using a Gemstone

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.380
to show entertainment broadcasts.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:10.970
Entertainment broadcasts over Gemstone?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.550
He comes from another world,

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:17.100
so he wondered out loud
with a straight face

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:20.520
if the relationship between
monsters and demons here

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.060
was no different than animals and people.

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:26.440
Huh? He can't be serious.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:31.070
Monsters and demons have the same
relationship as animals and people?

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.950
I've never even thought about it that way.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:36.120
One can't help but say

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:39.910
that the way he sees the world is
very different from the rest of us.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.660
Yeah.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:45.380
Also, he proposed a secret alliance.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:47.210
A secret alliance?

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:54.380
Yes. Souma promised that he
would walk in step with the empire.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:17:00.270
He also proposed a secret alliance,
in which the empire would defend the west,

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:04.140
while the kingdom would be
responsible for defending the east.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:09.820
Sister! I don't think this is
anything to be laughing at.

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:14.610
I'm sorry. But it's just so funny!

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:15.950
It's funny?

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.620
Well I mean, a country
that was so in decline

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:23.080
that up until just recently, we had
to be extra mindful toward them,

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:25.580
is all of a sudden such
good friends with us

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:29.790
that we can entrust the whole
eastern half of the continent to them!

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:34.670
It's almost as though a fairy has
cast a spell of illusion, isn't it?

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:39.180
Things certainly are moving at
a dizzying pace, aren't they?

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:43.100
Yes, indeed they are, Jeanne.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:48.810
Say, do you remember who the hero
is said to be in the kingdom?

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:50.820
It was in the report.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:54.110
"One who will lead the revolution
into a new age," wasn't it?

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:57.410
Yes. Not "One who will
defeat the Demon Lord,"

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.330
nor "One who will rule the world."

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:04.910
It's true, it doesn't quite feel
right to call him a "hero."

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:10.500
When you consider all
the hectic changes lately,

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.460
it does indeed feel like a "revolution"
is happening, doesn't it?

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:25.730
This man appears to be more
fascinating than I imagined.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:29.770
Ah, I can't wait to speak to him directly.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:41.370
I didn't think that you'd be coming, too.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:46.370
Well of course he'd be here!
After all, he's a fellow adventurer.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:51.080
Yuno, you said you just ran
into him at the guild.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:53.630
Sure you didn't twist his arm
to get him to come?

00:18:56.590 --> 00:19:00.720
Adventurers one and all,
welcome to Parnam Castle.

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:07.680
I am the fiancée of this country's
King Souma, Liscia Elfrieden.

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:09.440
I am here tonight in place of Souma,

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:12.440
who was unable to attend
due to his schedule,

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.730
so that I might say a few words.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:19.740
I want to thank you very much
for taking on this latest request.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:24.740
It is thanks to you that many of
our people's lives were saved.

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:30.620
On behalf of the absent Souma,
as well as the people of the kingdom,

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.000
I extend our gratitude.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.170
And with that, cheers!

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:37.550
Cheers!

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.760
Ah, Augus!

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:45.140
Leave a little <i>tatsuta-age</i>
for the rest of us!

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:54.520
I've been doing some thinking
after what happened, and...

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:59.360
...there's a good chance that
flame pierrot scare was made up--

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:04.120
Don't be such a party-pooper.
These octopus skewers are delicious.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.370
Dece, "ahh."

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.540
My mouth's already full!

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:12.370
Julia, are you drunk already?

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:17.500
What if I am? This is a benefit banquet
for adventurers, hosted by the kingdom.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:31.640
Come on, Master Mascot, you drink up, too.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:39.900
Drink, or I'll serve it
to you mouth-to-mouth.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:44.740
Okay, then. Let's drink as
much as we can tonight!

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:48.030
Yeah, we owe you a debt of gratitude.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:55.330
Quit wearing that outfit all the time
and have a drink with us!

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.170
No charge!

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:05.010
Whoa, are you okay, Master?
Are you that averse to liquor?

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:07.470
Master? Are you okay?

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:09.060
Please excuse me.

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:13.180
P-P-Princess Liscia?!

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:19.610
You almost gave yourself away.

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:21.530
I'll take it from here.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:24.780
O-Okay...

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:43.130
Um, is there something on my face,
or something?

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:47.800
Mm-mm, it's nothing.
All right, please enjoy yourself.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:54.430
That was a close one.

00:21:54.430 --> 00:21:57.520
Why did you join them if you
didn't want to get found out?

00:21:57.520 --> 00:22:00.110
Hiding inside your costume and everything?

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:05.400
What choice did I have?
Even I need to socialize sometimes.

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:12.740
By the way, was that Yuno?
She's pretty cute, huh?

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:17.210
Th-There's nothing funny
going on there! Oh!

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:21.710
I wasn't really asking if there was.

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:39.100
<i>"What are we supposed to choose?"</i>

00:22:39.100 --> 00:22:44.360
<i>Our voices imploring the future are hoarse</i>

00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:50.450
<i>We've become so afraid</i>
<i>of what we could lose</i>

00:22:50.450 --> 00:22:55.410
<i>that we're just frozen in place</i>

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:59.870
<i>How many times have we made mistakes</i>

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:05.840
<i>because we wanted to check our "answers"?</i>

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:13.180
<i>Before we knew it we were in love,</i>
<i>we had fallen in love</i>

00:23:13.180 --> 00:23:17.430
<i>I'll hold fast to you</i>
<i>in the times we're in</i>

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:23.230
<i>We who set alight</i>
<i>our finite lives to fight</i>

00:23:23.230 --> 00:23:28.490
<i>are noble and beautiful above all</i>

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:32.450
<i>As long as we create</i>
<i>as many bright tomorrows</i>

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.790
<i>as the indelible wounds we suffer,</i>

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:46.840
<i>we can be proud of all</i>
<i>we've woven together</i>
